---
import StandaloneGuide from '../../components/StandaloneGuide.astro';
const sections = [
  { heading:'Split the list into personal, shared and destination-specific', body:'Most group-trip overpacking happens because everyone packs as if they are traveling alone. Start with three buckets: what each person needs personally, what the group only needs one of, and what depends on the destination or rental.', bullets:['Personal: clothes, toiletries, medication, chargers','Shared: speaker, cooler, games, coffee supplies, first-aid basics','Destination-specific: beach towels, hiking gear, rain layers, ski accessories'] },
  { heading:'Assign shared items to actual people', body:'A shared packing list only works when each item has an owner. “Someone bring a cooler” is easy to ignore. “Sam: cooler” is clear. Keep the shared list short and confirm it the day before departure.' },
  { heading:'Check the rental before packing duplicates', body:'If you are staying in a house or condo, look closely at what is already provided. Hair dryers, beach towels, coffee makers, grills, laundry detergent and kitchen basics can remove a surprising amount from the group list.' },
  { heading:'Use one small arrival bag for the first few hours', body:'If the group is arriving at different times or cannot check in immediately, keep essentials accessible. A small day bag with medication, chargers, swimwear or weather layers can prevent everyone from opening luggage in a parking lot.' }
];
const checklist=['Personal medication','Chargers and power bank','Weather-appropriate layers','Shoes for planned activities','Shared-item assignments','Rental amenities checked','Travel documents or tickets','Small arrival-day bag','Reusable water bottle','One backup plan for weather'];
const mistakes=['Everyone bringing the same shared item','Assuming the rental has something without checking','Packing for activities that are only vague possibilities','Leaving shared-item assignments until departure morning','Putting medication or travel documents in checked or hard-to-reach luggage','Packing only for the forecasted high temperature'];
const faqs=[{q:'What should be on a group trip packing list?',a:'Separate personal essentials, shared group items and destination-specific gear. Assign each shared item to one person so duplicates and forgotten supplies are less likely.'},{q:'How do you avoid overpacking for a friends trip?',a:'Check what the lodging already provides, plan outfits around actual activities and share bulky items like coolers, speakers or games instead of duplicating them.'},{q:'What should one person bring for the whole group?',a:'Good shared candidates include a cooler, speaker, card games, basic first-aid supplies, coffee setup items and destination-specific gear that the group can share.'}];
---
<StandaloneGuide slug="group-trip-packing-list" category="group travel" title="Group Trip Packing List | Personal + Shared Weekend Checklist" description="A practical group trip packing list that separates personal essentials, shared supplies and destination-specific gear so friends do not overpack or forget the basics." h1="A group trip packing list that stops six people from bringing six coolers and zero bottle openers." intro="Packing for a group trip is different from packing solo. The useful question is not only what you need personally, but what the whole group needs exactly once. A simple personal-versus-shared system cuts duplicate gear and makes forgotten items easier to prevent." quickAnswer="Make three lists: personal essentials, shared group items and destination-specific gear. Assign every shared item to one person and check the rental amenities before packing duplicates." relatedDownload="group-trip-planner-printable" relatedLabel="Group Trip Planner Printable" {sections} {checklist} {mistakes} {faqs} relatedGuides={[{href:'/guides/group-trip-itinerary-planning/',label:'How to plan a group trip itinerary'},{href:'/guides/group-trip-budget-split/',label:'How to split group trip costs'}]} />
